    {
      "id": "claim_0d8574c6717049c2b9b514639210ae5f",
      "statement": "The wire formats are: SDP encoded via sdp-compact plus URL-safe substitutions (/ -> _, + -> ~, = -> -); offer link ?s=<offerSDP> plus optional i (ICE server override — the sender emits resolveIceServer(sendOptions.iceServer), i.e. the built-in STUN allowlist or a well-formed stun:/turn: custom URL, and the receive side accepts it only when it passes the same shared isSupportedIceServer predicate, else the default ICE server is used with an error toast), c (chunk size, validated against CHUNK_SIZE_OPTIONS with 32 KB fallback), and p (base64 RSA public key, encryption only; a malformed key downgrades the session to plaintext with an error toast); answer code <encodedAnswerSDP>|<base64 RSA public key or empty>, where an empty key portion is the receiver's deliberate plaintext downgrade and is handled, not treated as malformed. sdpDecode throws synchronously on empty, invalid-base64, or non-SDP input, so both user-controllable decode sites (the s link param and the answer code) are guarded with try/catch and surface an error toast instead of crashing the page (PR #45).",
      "evidence": [
